<title>AUSTRIA: Lenzing sees 1997 loss above 1996's.</title>
<headline>Lenzing sees 1997 loss above 1996's.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian fibre-maker Lenzing said on Friday it expected losses in the current year to exceed last year's amid continuing weak market conditions.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect the 1997 group loss to exceed that of 1996,&quot; chief executive Heinrich Stepniczka told Reuters in an interview. He declined to specify last year's total loss.  </p>
<p>&quot;We will not manage to achieve a profit just by raising prices,&quot; he added. &quot;Only in 1998 can we expect profits on the back of rationalisation measures, even if we remain at today's price level.&quot;</p>
<p>Lenzing in August reported a net loss of 85.7 million schillings for the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
